E-Commerce Sales Analytics Dashboard

Project Overview

This project is an interactive E-Commerce Sales Analytics Dashboard built using Microsoft Power BI. It analyzes sales, profit, quantity, product performance, customer segments, regional sales, and shipping trends to support data-driven business decisions.

Business Objectives

* Monitor sales, profit, quantity, and profit margin.
* Compare current year-to-date performance with the previous year.
* Analyze monthly sales and profit trends.
* Identify top-performing product categories and products.
* Understand sales distribution across customer regions.
* Analyze sales contribution by shipping type.
* Compare performance across customer segments.

Dashboard Features

KPI Summary

The dashboard includes key performance indicators for YTD Sales, YoY Sales, YTD Profit, YoY Profit, YTD Quantity, YoY Quantity, YTD Profit Margin, and YoY Profit Margin.

Monthly Trends

Monthly charts help analyze sales per order, profit per order, order quantity, and profit margin over time.

Category Performance

A comparison table displays category-level sales performance, previous-year sales, year-over-year changes, and trends.

Product Performance

Product-level charts help identify products contributing most to sales.

Geographic Analysis

A map visualizes sales distribution across customer regions and supports geographic performance analysis.

Shipping Analysis

A donut chart shows the distribution of sales across different shipping types.

Customer Segment Analysis

An interactive slicer allows users to filter the dashboard by customer segment.

Tools and Technologies

* Microsoft Power BI
* DAX
* Data Modeling
* Data Visualization
* Interactive Dashboards
* Business Intelligence

Business Questions

1. How are sales and profits performing compared with the previous year?
2. Which months show the strongest sales and profit performance?
3. Which product categories generate the highest sales?
4. Which products contribute most to overall sales?
5. How does sales performance vary across regions?
6. What is the sales distribution across shipping types?
7. How does performance differ between customer segments?

Business Value

The dashboard consolidates key business metrics into a single interactive report, helping users monitor performance, compare sales trends, evaluate products and categories, and identify areas requiring further analysis.

How to Use

1. Download the Power BI project file from this repository.
2. Open it in Microsoft Power BI Desktop.
3. Use the available filters and visual interactions to explore the data.
4. Compare KPI values and monthly trends to understand business performance. 

